' Roku performance beacons mark launch-timing milestones for the Roku OS. They
' are production telemetry signals used by Roku to measure when a channel
' becomes usable and to distinguish channel work from time spent waiting for the
' user.
'
' AppLaunchComplete means Starfin has reached its usable initial destination.
' For a normal launch that is Home. For a deep link it may be active playback or
' a rendered season. A failed deep link completes launch when its Home fallback is
' ready. Runtime input received after startup must not emit this signal again.
'
' AppDialogInitiate and AppDialogComplete surround launch-blocking interaction.
' "Dialog" is Roku's terminology and does not require a SceneGraph Dialog node.
' Starfin's full-screen login, saved-account selection, password entry, and
' Quick Connect flow qualify because startup must wait for the user to finish
' them.
'
' These signals contain no information about the UI, credentials, selection, or
' authentication result; they only identify the waiting-time boundary.
'
' This namespace does not call Roku APIs, control navigation, or send Jellyfin
' analytics. It owns only the state needed to return correctly paired Roku
' beacon names and to return an empty string for duplicate or post-launch
' signals.
'
' MainScene remains responsible for passing non-empty names to signalBeacon().
namespace PerformanceBeacon

    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ' PerformanceBeacon.Create
    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    function Create() as object
        return { launchComplete: false, dialogOpen: false }
    end function

    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ' PerformanceBeacon.BeginDialog
    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    function BeginDialog(state as object) as string
        if state.launchComplete or state.dialogOpen then return ""
        state.dialogOpen = true
        return "AppDialogInitiate"
    end function

    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ' PerformanceBeacon.CompleteDialog
    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    function CompleteDialog(state as object) as string
        if state.dialogOpen <> true then return ""
        state.dialogOpen = false
        return "AppDialogComplete"
    end function

    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ' PerformanceBeacon.CompleteLaunch
    '---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    function CompleteLaunch(state as object) as string
        if state.launchComplete then return ""
        state.launchComplete = true
        return "AppLaunchComplete"
    end function

end namespace
